e relic carrier  makes it back to the portal everybody  should walk through and immediately stop  so that the relic carrier can cleanse  the other two players who have been  whammied by a wacky blindness curse that  totally sucks called mark of the void  once everybody's cleansed it's time to  shift into a different formation team  sink plate books it to the right side to  do the sink plate thing all over again  team portal including the relic carrier  books it to the other portal to do the  portal thing all over again however one  player from each team peels off and runs  to the middle landing to defend the  newly spawned Conflux from the parade of  minotaurs sashay down the stairs now  you've got three teams of two team  conflux killing minotaurs team sink  plate keeping the portal up and killing  anything nearby and team portal heading  off to kill another gatekeeper and grab  another row team portal has the toughest  job but with judicious use of supers and  heavy weaponry not to mention a cleanse  when needed they should be equal to the  task when the relic drops have the other  player pick it up now the two relic  carriers book it through the portal and  once they're through everyone groups up  near the conflicts in the center to kill  all the leftover enemies and complete  the stage  checkpoint activated now for the final  stretch which is a doozy like the fight  against the Templar killing a Theon is  all about perfecting a cycle you'll need  two teams team portal and team homefront  team homefront sticks around to keep  both sync plates active and kill the  kamikaze harpies that a Theon spawns put  one player on each sink plate pillar and  have them kill harpies with vigor and  enthusiasm the third player needs to  also kill harpies by lending support to  whichever teammate needs it if you hop  up on the left portal frame there's this  ledge you can reach that keeps you out  of a Theon's line of fire and gives you  over watch on both positions when a  Theon is spawning harpies though he  won't shoot at you so you can drop down  to the top of the portal and kill  harpies it will keep this up until team  portal returns speaking of whom team  portal which includes the relic holder  must start the eighth Aeon phase and  each subsequent cycle as far back in the  room as possible a Theon always  teleports the three players that are  farthest from him and you want to be the  same team every time one steam portal is  beamed up they will arrive in one of two  areas jungle or desert jungle is a  little trickier because there's a minute  are waiting for you at the bottom that  you need to prioritize killing but the  approach to both is generally the same  rush down the stairs to the low center  platform taking potshots at the vex on  route once there the relic holder  focuses on killing the vex while the  other two kill the seven Oracle's as  they spawn yes Oracle's are back and yes  they still suck just as before Oracle  killing must proceed swiftly or else  everybody's gonna die 30 down  staying near the center of the circular  area allows you to see all the Oracles  and allows the relic holder to cleanse  you as needed once all the Oracles are  dead it's back through the portal to  reunite with team home front passing  back through the portal grants the whole  team above called times vengeance that  sounds super badass and boosts your  damage output but it's on a timer so you  need to make the most of it as soon as  team portal comes back everybody jumps  to the standalone platform between the  two sync plates the relic bearer will  put up a shield using l1 that blocks all  of a Theon's damage so make sure you are  entirely inside of it or you're going to  get blasted you might even need to duck  if you're near the edge so your head  doesn't peak out but once you're safely  inside it's time to go buckwild on the  big a for players with nasty sniper  rifles should aim for his glowing lower  abdominal section to land as many  critical hits as possible the relic  carrier keeps the shield up and the  sixth player kills as many harpies as  possible to clear everyone's retreat  once the times vengeance timer gets low  everybody hustles back to their starting  places team home front to the sink  plates and team portal to the back of  the room the relic bear should be the  last one to leave so that the shield can  cover the retreat and once everyone is  safely back in place the cycle begins  again and there you have it just execute  that plan flawlessly a bunch of times in  a row and you'll eventually be the  toughest destiny boss yet it's easier  said than done of course and if you're  having a really tough time of it  remember that these enemies including a  Theon are all level 28 so if you're  lower than that you're suffering a  damage penalty also like the Templar a  Theon has an enrage timer that you do  not want to trigger so cycle swiftly  stay alive and smite that shiny robot  devil thing I believe in you nay  gamespot believes in you some good luck  and happy raiding  you
 

